     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for adults:\n- **Immediate-release:** maximum 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- **Extended-release:** maximum 2,000 to 2,500 mg/day.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nCould you check what was intended? Possible corrections include:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals:** 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals:** 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 850 mg PO two or three times daily:** a common starting or titration dose.\n- **1,700 mg per day total:** for example, 850 mg PO twice daily.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with that note, though pharmacy will probably want to verify it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
